# Release signing — copy the four properties below into either
#   android/gradle.properties   (gitignored? CHECK — it is NOT, see note)
# or, better,
#   ~/.gradle/gradle.properties (outside the repo entirely)
#
# PREFER ~/.gradle/gradle.properties. android/gradle.properties IS tracked by
# git in this repo, so passwords put there will be committed. The keystore
# itself is safe either way (*.jks is gitignored), but the passwords are not.
#
# Without these, android/app/build.gradle falls back to DEBUG signing for
# release builds. That produces an AAB that looks fine and that Play will not
# accept. Pass -PCLOUDLYNK_REQUIRE_RELEASE_SIGNING=true to turn that silent
# fallback into a build failure — do this in CI and for anything going to Play.
#
# The keystore for this app is android/app/cloudlynk-release.jks. Its passwords
# were NOT included in the handover archive; get them from the owner. Losing
# the keystore or its passwords means the app can never be updated under the
# same Play listing without a Google-assisted key reset.

CLOUDLYNK_RELEASE_STORE_FILE=cloudlynk-release.jks
CLOUDLYNK_RELEASE_STORE_PASSWORD=
CLOUDLYNK_RELEASE_KEY_ALIAS=
CLOUDLYNK_RELEASE_KEY_PASSWORD=

# Path note: CLOUDLYNK_RELEASE_STORE_FILE is resolved by `file()` relative to
# android/app/, so a bare filename means android/app/<name>. An absolute path
# also works and is the right choice if you keep the keystore outside the repo.
